              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pellis, pellis — \"a hide, skin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pāstor pellem ovis vendit. The shepherd sells the sheep's hide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine, third declension. Mostly an animal's hide; cutis is skin as part of the body."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pellis is inherited from a Proto-Indo-European root meaning \"to cover, skin\" (EtymDB), and Old English fell \"hide\" is a cousin. English pellicle, a thin skin, comes from its diminutive."
            }
          ]
        },
